<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδρωψ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωπος</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>dropsy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.22
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).122.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				123.33
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				190
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.37
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕ. ξηρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Aph.</u>
					4.11
				</span></i>
			; he distinguishes two kinds, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ
				ὑποσαρκίδιος</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τῇ σαρκί</span>
			) and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μετ᾽ ἐμφυσημάτων,</span>
			<i>Acut.(Sp.</i>)<i><span class="en">
				52
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕ, εἰς ἀμίδα</span>”
				<i>diabetes,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					7.81
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>any watery discharge,</i> e.g. <i>discharge before
				parturition,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				587a6
			</span></i>, Cleophant. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				2.53
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόφορος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a dropsical person,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Int.</u>
				47
			</span></i> (dub. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epid.</u>
				2.5.13
			</span></i>— in which sense <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.148
			</span></i> read <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδρώψ</span> (oxyt.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> one of the four
			humours, <i>aqueous humour,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Morb.</u>
				4.32
			</span></i>, al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
